From sunlight to irrigation, green technology is helping Ghanaian farmers grow more.

In Ghana, the Aveyime smart solar irrigation project, implemented by CECEP CGC, uses a 100-kilowatt distributed smart solar irrigation system to provide water on demand. 

The project has cut farmers' electricity costs by 80 percent, supplies 200,000 cubic meters of water annually, reduces carbon emissions by 40 metric tons a year, and boosts rice yields to 1.5 times.

More than solving irrigation challenges in one area, the Aveyime project offers a sustainable approach to using green technology to increase agricultural productivity, support poverty reduction in local communities, and protect the environment. 
